hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"138","On the authority of Muhammad bin Yahya, on the authority of Ahmad bin Khalid al-Wahbi, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Muhammad bin Yahya bin Hibban, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Abdullah Ibn Omar said: I said: Ibn Omar performed ablution for every prayer, whether he was pure or impure. Who is that? He said: It was narrated to him by Asma’ bint Zayd ibn al-Khattab, that Abdullah ibn Hanzalah ibn Abi Amir narrated to her, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace “He ordered one to perform ablution for every prayer, whether pure or impure. When this became difficult for him, he ordered the siwak to be used for every prayer.” Ibn Umar believed that he had the strength to do that, so he did not skip ablution for every prayer."
